Open questions for the integrator (do not guess at implementation time):
1. Whether `warehouseLayerName` should actually resolve to a real
   `geo.layers.name`/`SLIDER_STREAM_LAYER_NAMES`/`SNAPSHOT_SURFACE_LAYER_NAMES` entry, or stay
   null because the collecting-event window is not the global day slider (see spec's "must not
   reuse a daily environmental slider" constraint). This slice assumes null; the shared owner must
   confirm this doesn't silently drop the layer per the §9 LEFT JOIN warning in layer-registry.ts.
2. Whether the map/layer-render-contract.ts and parquet-slider-capabilities.ts need new members at
   all, given (1) — if warehouseLayerName stays null, no capability entry is needed for the day
   axis, but the occurrence plane's own bbox/zoom/release-set query still needs a route. This
   slice calls the agri-data-service directly (see src/lib/botanical-occurrences.ts's module doc);
   the integrator may prefer a Next.js proxy route instead.
